---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Boxifu, an academic and game developer portfolio."
>
  <section class="section page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Academic curiosity with a game developer's eye for systems.</h1>
    <p>
      This page is the home for a fuller biography, research interests, education, teaching, tools, and creative practice.
      The first version keeps the structure ready without pretending to know details that should come directly from you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section content-columns" aria-label="About details">
    <article>
      <h2>Research and academic work</h2>
      <p>
        Use this section for research areas, publications, conference work, lab affiliations, or teaching experience.
        Keeping it in page content makes it easy to revise as your academic work evolves.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Game development</h2>
      <p>
        Use this section for engines, design interests, prototypes, shipped work, team roles, and the kinds of player
        experiences you care about building.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Technical practice</h2>
      <p>
        Use this section for programming languages, tools, systems work, production workflows, and maintainability values.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
